261
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:31,917
Stay quiet or say a few words.

262
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:32,830
It doesn't matter.

263
00:13:32,913 --> 00:13:34,329
You're still going to die.

264
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:37,290
Listen!

265
00:13:37,540 --> 00:13:40,360
I'm the man who'll be king of the pirates!

266
00:13:41,900 --> 00:13:44,800
I'm the man who'll be king of the pirates!

267
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:48,490
What?

268
00:13:49,380 --> 00:13:51,200
He's the king of the pirates.

269
00:13:51,900 --> 00:13:54,157
In this town of all places?

270
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:56,060
That's a crazy thing to say.

271
00:13:56,740 --> 00:13:59,740
We're finally getting to
the best part of the show.

272
00:13:59,860 --> 00:14:00,800
Bye-bye now.

273
00:14:04,180 --> 00:14:05,800
Stop the execution!

274
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:07,490
Now!

275
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:13,880
Saatchi! Zoro!

276
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:15,950
No!

277
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:17,532
It's Pirate Hunter Zoro!

278
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:20,830
Zoro?

279
00:14:22,180 --> 00:14:25,660
You made it, Zoro, but you're
just a little bit too late.

280
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,118
We're gonna break down the platform!

281
00:14:31,140 --> 00:14:32,280
Boronor, Zoro.

282
00:14:35,100 --> 00:14:36,860
Okay, boys, get him!

283
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:38,180
Let's do it!

284
00:14:53,900 --> 00:14:56,560
Not even the Great Zoro can stop me now!

285
00:14:56,880 --> 00:14:58,760
There's nothing you two can do!

286
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,765
It's the end for your captain!

287
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:02,690
Bastard!

288
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:08,680
If I can just cut down the platform...

289
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:10,530
Listen!

290
00:15:10,613 --> 00:15:11,760
The moment Monkey D.

291
00:15:11,900 --> 00:15:14,520
Luffy's head falls, we
all attack together!

292
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:19,620
Prepare for battle, sir!

293
00:15:24,560 --> 00:15:27,380
Nami, hurry up! Nami! Heavy! Sorry.

294
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:31,280
But I'm dead.

295
00:15:33,460 --> 00:15:34,290
Idiot!

296
00:15:35,860 --> 00:15:36,760
Don't say that.

297
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:38,540
He smiled.

298
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:28,820
I'm still alive!

299
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:30,420
That's nice.

300
00:16:36,220 --> 00:16:38,240
That was divine intervention.

301
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:40,200
Stop talking nonsense.

302
00:16:40,620 --> 00:16:42,385
We gotta get out of this town.

303
00:16:42,620 --> 00:16:44,500
Our troubles are not over.

304
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:50,630
Attack!

305
00:16:50,713 --> 00:16:52,720
Surround all the pirates now!

306
00:16:56,580 --> 00:16:57,700
Here they come!

307
00:17:04,900 --> 00:17:05,730
Oh, wow!

308
00:17:05,813 --> 00:17:06,700
So cool!

309
00:17:07,740 --> 00:17:09,916
Everybody here went crazy so quickly!

310
00:17:10,540 --> 00:17:11,370
Lupin!

311
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:13,550
Zoro!

312
00:17:13,633 --> 00:17:14,657
We don't have time for this.

313
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:16,037
We've got to get out of here.

314
00:17:16,120 --> 00:17:17,897
We'd better hurry back to the Going Mary

315
00:17:17,980 --> 00:17:19,737
or we'll never be able
to leave this island.

316
00:17:19,820 --> 00:17:22,437
And we sure as hell won't
get to the Grand Round.

317
00:17:22,520 --> 00:17:23,350
Really?

318
00:17:23,433 --> 00:17:24,263
Well, that's no good.

319
00:17:24,346 --> 00:17:25,176
Run!

320
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:28,220
The Skrull Head gang is getting away!

321
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:30,310
Capture them!

322
00:17:35,140 --> 00:17:36,520
Why did he smile?

323
00:17:37,660 --> 00:17:39,460
Did he know he'd be saved?

324
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:42,190
No.

325
00:17:42,420 --> 00:17:46,720
At that moment, he was certain
that his life was about to end.

326
00:17:47,460 --> 00:17:51,500
He simply accepted death and
smiled after preparing himself.

327
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:54,214
Captain, we have to pursue the pirates!

328
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:55,713
Lieutenant, think back.

329
00:17:56,260 --> 00:18:00,260
Have you ever seen any pirates who
smiled on the execution platform?

330
00:18:01,780 --> 00:18:02,640
No, sir.

331
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:04,977
It doesn't matter how tough the guy is.

332
00:18:05,060 --> 00:18:08,557
At the moment of death, they all
turn pale and die in despair.

333
00:18:08,640 --> 00:18:10,640
That Straw Hat man smiled.

334
00:18:11,140 --> 00:18:12,080
I saw it.

335
00:18:13,220 --> 00:18:16,657
He smiled just like
Gold Roger 22 years ago

336
00:18:16,740 --> 00:18:19,597
just like the old king of the pirates did.

337
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:22,820
On that exact execution platform.

338
00:18:34,260 --> 00:18:37,537
Captain where's the
Straw Hat man now sir he

339
00:18:37,620 --> 00:18:40,561
slipped past us and is
heading towards the harbor?

340
00:18:43,100 --> 00:18:45,797
Unit 1 should have
destroyed their ship by now.

341
00:18:45,880 --> 00:18:49,080
Well, sir, they had to return
to port for a refitting.

342
00:18:49,320 --> 00:18:52,337
See, they couldn't light their
powder due to the sudden rain.

343
00:18:52,420 --> 00:18:53,250
What?

344
00:18:53,980 --> 00:18:58,277
But a reserve unit is currently making
preparations to attack the ship instead.

345
00:18:58,360 --> 00:19:00,537
Captain Smoker, if we let them sail now,

346
00:19:00,620 --> 00:19:04,477
they'll be able to get to the Grand
Line before we can capture them.

347
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:06,900
The wind is blowing towards the west.

348
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:09,380
It's a tailwind for that ship.

349
00:19:11,140 --> 00:19:13,160
Is this just mere coincidence?

350
00:19:15,600 --> 00:19:19,424
It's as if heaven itself has
special plans for this young pirate.

351
00:19:20,600 --> 00:19:23,260
We'd better picket the
pace or we're toast!

352
00:19:23,840 --> 00:19:25,860
I am White Hunter Smoker.

353
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:32,180
On my honor as Marine Captain, I
won't let that man leave this island.

354
00:19:37,540 --> 00:19:39,617
What the hell is up with all this rain?

355
00:19:39,700 --> 00:19:41,197
Nami was right about this storm.

356
00:19:41,280 --> 00:19:43,397
If we don't get back to
the ship and set sail soon,

357
00:19:43,480 --> 00:19:45,715
we're going to be stuck here for good.

358
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:50,365
You're wasting your time,
you silly little man.

359
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:55,092
There isn't anybody alive who can lay
a hand on this perfectly smooth skin.

360
00:19:58,480 --> 00:19:59,520
That was weird.

361
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:01,157
I saw a field of flowers.

362
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:04,580
Captain Buggy, you're not
fried to a crisp! I don't die!

363
00:20:04,860 --> 00:20:05,877
This isn't good, Buggy!

364
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:07,477
They're sending Marines from Headquarters!

365
00:20:07,560 --> 00:20:08,678
They'll never stop!

366
00:20:08,800 --> 00:20:11,506
Heh, I don't care, they
can stick their noses!

367
00:20:11,660 --> 00:20:13,200
Don't let me say noses!

368
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:14,560
Ugh, my bad!

369
00:20:16,700 --> 00:20:17,530
Huh?

370
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:19,310
What now?

371
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:21,677
We go after that little rubber twerk!

372
00:20:21,760 --> 00:20:23,957
Moji and Richie are burning
his ship as we speak,

373
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:25,497
so he's got no place he can run to?

374
00:20:25,580 --> 00:20:29,037
so all that's left for us to do
is do what Buggy pirates do best!

375
00:20:29,120 --> 00:20:30,320
Kick his ass! Yeah!

376
00:20:31,020 --> 00:20:32,140
Ha ha! Motor!

377
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:33,420
Yeah, Captain!

378
00:20:35,780 --> 00:20:37,460
Chouchou buggy!

379
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:39,640
Bomb engine, ignite!

380
00:20:42,140 --> 00:20:44,220
Set the ramp, now!

381
00:20:44,600 --> 00:20:46,140
Right track is set!

382
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:47,580
No friction!

383
00:20:50,060 --> 00:20:52,040
Smooth, smooth track!

384
00:20:58,140 --> 00:21:00,440
Don't let those pirates escape!

385
00:21:07,160 --> 00:21:09,020
Where did the smoke come from?

386
00:21:11,940 --> 00:21:13,320
What is it?

387
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:14,580
Whiteout time!

388
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:20,440
Smoker!

389
00:21:22,040 --> 00:21:24,820
I can't waste my time
with you little fools.

390
00:21:25,660 --> 00:21:26,720
So strong.

391
00:21:26,980 --> 00:21:28,937
So that's the power of
the Plum Plum Fruit.

392
00:21:29,020 --> 00:21:31,785
He took out Buggy's entire
crew just like that.

393
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:34,310
Fire!

394
00:21:41,100 --> 00:21:43,140
Smoker, you bastard!

395
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:46,720
I can't break free of
this horrible steel net.

396
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:48,897
Where'd they get a gun like that?

397
00:21:48,980 --> 00:21:54,160
It's a cage shot developed by the Marines
to deal with Devil Fruit powers, cowards.

398
00:21:56,100 --> 00:21:57,600
I'll get the Straw Hat.

399
00:21:57,860 --> 00:21:59,660
Bring my billower pipe. Sir!

400
00:22:03,380 --> 00:22:04,700
Dammit! Crap!

401
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:06,797
Why did it have to start storming now?

402
00:22:06,880 --> 00:22:10,115
How am I supposed to burn
down this ship when it's wet?

403
00:22:12,740 --> 00:22:13,837
Aw, man, Richie,

404
00:22:13,920 --> 00:22:16,917
we're gonna get in big trouble if we
can't get a fire going in this rain.

405
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:17,830
One more try.

406
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:23,591
Relax, Ritchie, I'll feed you in a minute.

407
00:22:25,460 --> 00:22:26,640
What are you doing?

408
00:22:28,020 --> 00:22:28,850
Moji!

409
00:22:30,660 --> 00:22:32,719
Well, if it isn't the little thief.

410
00:22:34,100 --> 00:22:35,140
Go, Ritchie!

411
00:22:42,560 --> 00:22:44,540
Special attack, fresh egg star!

412
00:22:52,260 --> 00:22:54,540
Damn brain, it made my hand slip!

413
00:22:58,120 --> 00:22:58,950
Richie!

414
00:22:59,200 --> 00:23:00,700
I'll feed you later!

415
00:23:01,900 --> 00:23:03,220
Good, now let's go!

416
00:23:04,180 --> 00:23:05,600
Not so fast!

417
00:23:05,840 --> 00:23:07,252
You have to get past me!

418
00:23:07,760 --> 00:23:09,320
My name is Moji!

419
00:23:09,660 --> 00:23:14,484
I am a proud buggy pirate, and I won't let
you get anywhere near this stupid ship!

420
00:23:15,720 --> 00:23:17,320
Get ready to fire!

421
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:19,200
Marines!

422
00:23:19,820 --> 00:23:21,060
Bad aim!

423
00:23:23,120 --> 00:23:23,950
Fire!

424
00:23:28,940 --> 00:23:31,000
Go contact the cannon unit.

425
00:23:31,300 --> 00:23:33,237
We have to capture this pirate vessel.

426
00:23:33,320 --> 00:23:34,540
Sir! Nami!

427
00:23:35,060 --> 00:23:35,960
I know!

428
00:23:44,340 --> 00:23:46,180
Damn this storm.

429
00:23:48,100 --> 00:23:50,440
Which way is this sea? I don't know.

430
00:23:50,620 --> 00:23:53,017
The rain makes it hard to
tell where we're going.

431
00:23:53,100 --> 00:23:53,982
There they are!

432
00:23:56,220 --> 00:23:57,637
Damn, they're like roaches.

433
00:23:57,720 --> 00:23:58,997
You want to stop and fight them?

434
00:23:59,080 --> 00:24:00,551
There's no time for that.

435
00:24:02,260 --> 00:24:03,240
Oh, wow!

436
00:24:03,540 --> 00:24:04,660
Who is that?

437
00:24:06,680 --> 00:24:09,820
I didn't know you were
Zoro and a pirate as well.

438
00:24:10,780 --> 00:24:12,420
Found one right here.

439
00:24:14,520 --> 00:24:15,500
You lied.

440
00:24:16,420 --> 00:24:19,520
You're just another liar! Oh, great!

441
00:24:19,700 --> 00:24:21,517
What the hell did you do to that girl?

442
00:24:21,600 --> 00:24:24,247
You never asked me what
my name was, did you?

443
00:24:24,900 --> 00:24:26,620
So I never lied, did I?

444
00:24:27,480 --> 00:24:29,857
You know there's no way
I'm going to allow someone

445
00:24:29,940 --> 00:24:32,457
like you to leave town with
such a legendary sword!

446
00:24:32,540 --> 00:24:33,370
Give it to me!

447
00:24:33,460 --> 00:24:35,540
The Wadoichi Manji! Right now!

448
00:24:42,820 --> 00:24:43,650
Okay.

449
00:24:44,580 --> 00:24:45,860
What a jerk!

450
00:24:46,060 --> 00:24:47,413
You can't fight a girl!

451
00:24:47,660 --> 00:24:48,601
Get out of here.

452
00:24:49,960 --> 00:24:50,790
Let's go!

453
00:24:53,240 --> 00:24:56,760
Hey, Zoro, if you hurt her,
I'm gonna kick your ass!

454
00:24:57,600 --> 00:24:58,740
Toshigi's got one!

455
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:19,765
I hate to disappoint, but you
will never get this sword from me.

456
00:25:20,340 --> 00:25:22,180
I can't believe she's lost.

457
00:25:22,480 --> 00:25:24,380
I've never seen her lose before.

458
00:25:25,700 --> 00:25:27,759
Now I think it's time for me to go.

459
00:25:32,180 --> 00:25:34,000
Why didn't you kill me?

460
00:25:35,140 --> 00:25:36,040
I know.

461
00:25:36,300 --> 00:25:37,712
It's because I'm a girl.

462
00:25:39,760 --> 00:25:40,960
You're lucky, Zoro.

463
00:25:41,280 --> 00:25:42,480
Being born as a man.

464
00:25:43,900 --> 00:25:46,897
It's pathetic that you can't
fight me because I'm a woman.

465
00:25:46,980 --> 00:25:48,039
It's embarrassing!

466
00:25:49,080 --> 00:25:52,237
You may be physically stronger,
but you don't have the guts.

467
00:25:52,320 --> 00:25:54,277
This sword isn't just for decoration.

468
00:25:54,360 --> 00:25:57,831
I don't even think you know
what it means to carry a sword.

469
00:25:59,360 --> 00:26:01,301
Would you shut up for one second?

470
00:26:03,200 --> 00:26:06,877
Look, you got the same face as some
girl I knew who died a long time ago,

471
00:26:06,960 --> 00:26:09,437
and before I know a thing about
you, you're talking just like her.

472
00:26:09,520 --> 00:26:12,777
What I want you to do is stop acting like
some dead person you don't even know.

473
00:26:12,860 --> 00:26:14,213
And try to be yourself.

474
00:26:14,820 --> 00:26:16,477
Excuse the hell out of me.

475
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:18,897
It's not my fault I sound
like your dead girlfriend.

476
00:26:18,980 --> 00:26:20,697
I had no idea it was so rude.

477
00:26:20,780 --> 00:26:22,357
And thoughtless of me to be myself.

478
00:26:22,440 --> 00:26:23,270
You jerk.

479
00:26:23,353 --> 00:26:25,004
You ever think before you talk?

480
00:26:26,440 --> 00:26:27,580
What'd you say?

481
00:26:28,220 --> 00:26:29,537
I see the ship.

482
00:26:29,620 --> 00:26:31,400
The harbor is up ahead.

483
00:26:36,780 --> 00:26:37,610
Great.

484
00:26:37,693 --> 00:26:38,680
Now what?

485
00:26:41,360 --> 00:26:43,677
Straw Hat Luffy.

486
00:26:43,760 --> 00:26:46,340
You're finally here.

487
00:26:59,780 --> 00:27:00,897
Destiny.

488
00:27:00,980 --> 00:27:02,057
Fate.

489
00:27:02,140 --> 00:27:03,377
Dreams.

490
00:27:03,460 --> 00:27:06,017
These unstoppable ideals.

491
00:27:06,100 --> 00:27:08,257
Are held deep in the heart of man.

492
00:27:08,340 --> 00:27:11,940
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

493
00:27:12,220 --> 00:27:14,867
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

494
00:27:15,720 --> 00:27:18,120
The Pirate King, fine by me.

495
00:27:25,740 --> 00:27:27,940
I'm Captain Smoker of the Marines,

496
00:27:28,140 --> 00:27:30,677
and I'm in charge of keeping
the peace in this town.

497
00:27:30,760 --> 00:27:34,757
You're under arrest.
Huh? Arrest? Forget that.

498
00:27:34,840 --> 00:27:39,580
See, I'm going to the Grand Lines so
that I can become King of the Pirates.

499
00:27:39,740 --> 00:27:41,100
King of the Pirates?

500
00:27:41,240 --> 00:27:43,711
And I refuse to get arrested in this town.

501
00:27:43,820 --> 00:27:45,820
Then you'll have to go through me.

502
00:27:46,800 --> 00:27:47,700
Let's go.

503
00:27:49,120 --> 00:27:51,740
Sanji, I'll be right there. Go on.

504
00:27:59,420 --> 00:28:00,250
Fire!

505
00:28:06,120 --> 00:28:07,560
Get in, fire!

506
00:28:22,460 --> 00:28:26,578
If we stay here even a minute longer,
the Going Mary will be done for!

507
00:28:31,740 --> 00:28:33,357
You can't set sail yet!

508
00:28:33,440 --> 00:28:35,217
Luffy and the others aren't back!

509
00:28:35,300 --> 00:28:36,740
There's no other choice!

510
00:28:36,980 --> 00:28:38,862
If we stay here, she'll be sunk!

511
00:28:39,920 --> 00:28:41,060
Brightwater, fall!

512
00:28:44,800 --> 00:28:46,540
What about the rest of them?

513
00:28:46,720 --> 00:28:48,191
We'll pick them up later!

514
00:28:48,480 --> 00:28:49,657
Don't let them escape!

515
00:28:49,740 --> 00:28:51,460
After them! Nami!

516
00:28:52,300 --> 00:28:53,480
Huh? Sanji!

517
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:54,830
Sanji!

518
00:28:55,020 --> 00:28:56,700
Wait up, I'm back!

519
00:28:57,480 --> 00:28:58,715
Where are the others?

520
00:28:59,200 --> 00:29:00,520
Uh, who cares?

521
00:29:00,720 --> 00:29:02,249
We'll just get them later!

522
00:29:04,460 --> 00:29:06,220
Behind you! Look out!

523
00:29:12,500 --> 00:29:13,330
Dammit!

524
00:29:13,413 --> 00:29:14,301
This is endless!

525
00:29:14,660 --> 00:29:16,040
We have to get closer!

526
00:29:16,420 --> 00:29:20,057
But there's no way that we can take
the ship back against this current!

527
00:29:20,140 --> 00:29:20,970
Goddammit!

528
00:29:21,820 --> 00:29:22,900
Usai! Master!

529
00:29:34,140 --> 00:29:35,620
Saint, ooze up!

530
00:29:49,500 --> 00:29:50,820
What's happening?

531
00:29:51,380 --> 00:29:56,260
